  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 140 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nSaturday, morning showers and storms should wane, and drop south of \nthe area, with most of the middle of the day and evening rather \nquiet, before more storms potentially move in for the overnight \nours.  Again, deterministic CAMs are highly variable on timing and \nlocation, but all models show our area at the north periphery of a \nbroad warm, humid high pressure, and that supports strong MUCAPE and \nthe increasing flow aloft (mainly SW flow) supports some deep layer \nshear growing through the mid week period. SPC continues a level 1 \nrisk for our extreme southwest Saturday, followed by a Slight, Level \n2 risk for severe storms for our far western counties Monday. \n\nThe southwest flow appears to continue through at least mid week \nbefore a pattern change could occur, with a larger upper low \nbecoming absorbed into the strong zonal flow. That low is forecast \nto be in the Pac-Northwest US, before ejecting across the Plains as \nan open wave late in the week.",
